### Warnings Resolved in `build_project.tcl`
- **`[filemgmt 56-12]` (3 occurrences resolved)**:
  - *Representative Message*: `File 'C:/Agents/Day5/rtl/half_adder.v' cannot be added to the project because it already exists in the project, skipping this file`
  - *Cause*: The script executed `add_files` unconditionally outside the `if-else` branch. When opening an existing project (`open_project`), the files were already present in the project, causing Vivado to issue duplicate-file warnings.
  - *Correction*: Moved `add_files` and `update_compile_order` for `sources_1`, `sim_1`, and `constrs_1` inside the `else` block so they only run upon project creation. The target device (`xc7z010clg400-1`) and all design files were preserved.

---

### Remaining Warnings & Corrections Outside Script
1. **`[Board 49-26]` (83 occurrences remaining)**:
   - *Representative Message*: `cannot add Board Part xilinx.com:emb-plus-vpr-4616:part0:1.0 available at C:/Xilinx/2025.1/data/xhub/boards\XilinxBoardStore\boards\Xilinx\emb-plus-vpr-4616\1.0\board.xml as part xcve2302-sfva784-2mp-e-s specified in board_part file is either invalid or not available`
   - *Cause*: Vivado's global XHub Board Store catalog contains definitions for Versal devices (`xcve2302-...`) that are not installed in this Vivado installation. This scan occurs during Vivado environment initialization before user project commands execute.
   - *Correction outside script*: Install device support for the missing parts in Vivado or remove the incompatible board definition folders from the XHub Board Store directory (`C:/Xilinx/2025.1/data/xhub/boards/XilinxBoardStore`).

2. **`[Project 1-5713]` (1 occurrence remaining)**:
   - *Representative Message*: `Board part '' set for the project is not found. BoardPart property will be unset. Please select board from latest repo build`
   - *Cause*: The pre-existing project file (`fpga_demo.xpr`) contains an empty `BoardPart` property (`BoardPart=""`). Vivado parses the `.xpr` file and emits this warning directly inside `open_project` before subsequent script commands can intervene.
   - *Correction outside script*: Clean up or remove the invalid `BoardPart` attribute directly within the `fpga_demo.xpr` file, or recreate the project cleanly.

